  "body": "## Bayesian curl\n\nAdded as a fourth variation on **Cable Bicep Curl** (day 6): 13 lbs × 12 reps × 3 sets, alongside Standard / Rope Hammer / Single Arm.\n\nAlready upserted into Cosmos (`exercise-6-cable-bicep-curl`, partition `shared`) so it's live now; this commit keeps `seed-data.js` in sync so a fresh database init produces the same library.\n\nNote: that exercise's `notes` still read \"Reps to failure, decrease weight by 5-10 each time\", which describes the other three variations but not this one. Left alone — per-variation notes don't exist in the schema.\n\n## Variation chips\n\nThe chips were `text-slate-400` on `bg-slate-700/50` with a `border-slate-600/40` — dim gray pills that read as metadata tags, not controls. That's how the **Concentration** variation sat unnoticed on Dumbbell Bicep Curl.\n\nNow: a `VARIATION` label ahead of the row, full-contrast text on a visible border, `px-2.5 py-1` instead of `px-2 py-0.5` for a real tap target, and `aria-pressed` on the selected chip.\n\n## Verification\n\nDriven live against the dev server on day 6:\n\n```\nbefore: Cable Bicep Curl | VARIATION | Standard | Rope Hammer | Single Arm | Bayesian | Target: 20 lbs × Failure reps × 3 sets\nafter : Cable Bicep Curl(Bayesian) | VARIATION | ... | Target: 13 lbs × 12 reps × 3 sets\n```\n\n`npm run build` clean.\n\nAnonymous visitors read `snapshot.db`, so Bayesian reaches the public view after the next 4-hourly snapshot run.",
